# {{ company_prog_name }} — Help

Present the map below — Italian, founders' register: tight, no emoji.
Do NOT run any command to produce it; this is orientation, not a status
check (state is `/cs-review`'s job). Adapt phrasing freely, keep the
content exact.

## What this is

The customer-service operator for **{{ email_address }}**: this session
drives the mrcall-desktop engine (synced mail, relationship memory,
tasks, trained voice). It triages, drafts and advances campaigns;
nothing is sent without the operator's say-so (draft-first; the
autonomy dial is a deliberate later step).

## The commands (you type these)

| Command | When |
|---|---|
| `/cs-review` | sit-down bootstrap: what the operator prepared, what awaits you{% if producer_adapter != 'none' %}, the day's outreach candidates{% endif %} |
| `/cs-account <name>` | deep-dive on one account (read-only) |
| `/cs-cron` | the unattended tick: status, install/remove (confirmed), pause/resume |
| `/cs-campaign` | design a new campaign: pack + wiring, draft-first |
| `/cs-help` | this map |

## Or just ask

- *"what's new today?"* / *"what's still open in support mail?"*
- *"load customer X"* (docs + engine memory — before any customer work)
- *"draft a reply to X"* (a DRAFT lands in Gmail Drafts; you send)
- *"I called him, close this one"* (resolved off-email: it gets recorded, so
  the sweep stops re-raising it — reversible)
- *"find the document about Y"*

Behind those sit the operator skills (`cs-triage-mail`,
`cs-campaign-tick`, `cs-customer`, `cs-find-document`; `cs-operator` is
the headless cron bootstrap) — they fire on their own when the request
matches.

## The hard lines (always true)

- Draft-first: every outgoing mail is reviewed until send mode is
  deliberately enabled. Dedup (Gmail Sent truth), `RATE_CAP` and the
  dossier-before-contact rule are not negotiable.
- Kill-switch: `touch ~/.{{ company_slug }}-cs/CS_PAUSE` stops every
  automated tick; remove the file to resume.

